SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agioi Evlampios & Evlampia\, Amalou
LOCATION:Amalou\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Amalou\, a tiny stone village on the wild west coast below Vrakades\, hosts a 'big panigiri' on 10 August with the Zevkalides. It is one of the most atmospheric spots on the island to dance\, but the access road is rough and there is almost no parking\; go with one car per group. Faros (near the airport) and Steli/Platani celebrate the same night.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#amalou-panigiri-of-agioi-evlampios-evlampia-amalou
