BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-langada-panigiri-of-the-dormition-langada-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition\, Langada
LOCATION:Langada\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The most famous panigiri in Greece. In the near-abandoned village of Langada above Agios Dimitrios\, the Dormition draws people from across the island and the diaspora for an all-night feast that ends well after sunrise. Communal\, unhurried\, wine-and-dance till dawn — the clearest window into why Ikarians live so long.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#langada-panigiri-of-the-dormition-langada
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#langada-panigiri-of-the-dormition-langada
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-langada-panigiri-of-the-dormition-langada-2028@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20280815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20280816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition\, Langada
LOCATION:Langada\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The most famous panigiri in Greece. In the near-abandoned village of Langada above Agios Dimitrios\, the Dormition draws people from across the island and the diaspora for an all-night feast that ends well after sunrise. Communal\, unhurried\, wine-and-dance till dawn — the clearest window into why Ikarians live so long.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#langada-panigiri-of-the-dormition-langada
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#langada-panigiri-of-the-dormition-langada
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-gialiskari-seaside-panigiri-of-the-dormition-gialiskari-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Seaside panigiri of the Dormition\, Gialiskari
LOCATION:Gialiskari\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The fishing hamlet of Gialiskari next to Armenistis\, with its white chapel on the rocks\, celebrates 15 August right by the water\, organised by the cultural association 'I Koimisis': Ikarian wine\, goat and local dishes\, with Stroupa and the Zevkalides playing in 2023\, until morning. Ideal if you are based in Armenistis and do not want the Langada trek\; walk over along the beach.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#gialiskari-seaside-panigiri-of-the-dormition-gialiskari
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#gialiskari-seaside-panigiri-of-the-dormition-gialiskari
